{"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Relating Entities","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RelatingEntities","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Building Hierarchies","anchor":"Building-Hierarchies","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AncestorsView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/DescendantsView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/CyclicHierarchy","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/HierarchyError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some state belongs to a pair of entities rather than to one: a unit likes another, a turret aims"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at a ship, a button sits on a panel. A "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"relation","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" stores that kind of link, and the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"hierarchy","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the relation that makes trees of parents and children."}]},{"text":"Link Entities with Relations","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Link-Entities-with-Relations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a relation as a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation","type":"reference"},{"text":", then link a source entity to a target","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/relate(_:_:to:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and unlink it with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/unrelate(_:_:from:)","type":"reference"},{"text":". Read the links in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"either direction: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/targets(_:of:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" lists what a source relates to, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/sources(_:of:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" lists what relates to a target.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A relation can carry values, one per link, such as the amount one entity owes another. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chooses two behaviors with static properties:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/isExclusive"},{"type":"text","text":" limits a source to one target, so relating it to a new target"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaces the old one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/onTargetDespawn"},{"type":"text","text":" says what despawning a target does to its sources: remove their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"links, the default, or despawn them too."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A source holds its links in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","type":"reference"},{"text":" component, which you read and filter on like any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component. To visit only the sources of one target, filter a query with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".related(_:to:)"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses the world’s index of each target’s sources rather than walking every source.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Build a Hierarchy","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Build-a-Hierarchy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hierarchy is the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" relation: exclusive, so each entity has at most one parent, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"despawning a parent despawns its children, and theirs in turn. Spawn an entity under a parent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/spawn(_:childOf:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or move an existing one with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/addChild(_:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/CyclicHierarchy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" rather than make an entity its own ancestor. Walk the tree with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/parent(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/children(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/ancestors(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/descendants(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the hierarchy is a relation, the same query filters work on it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".related(ChildOf.self, to: ship)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" visits the children of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ship","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".without(Targets<ChildOf>.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" visits the roots.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example aims a ship’s turret at a comet, then at a moon, and despawns the ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its turret:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct AimsAt: Relation {","    static var isExclusive: Bool { true }","}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Name(value: \"ship\"))","let turret = world.spawn(Name(value: \"turret\"), childOf: ship)","let comet = world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"))","let moon = world.spawn(Name(value: \"moon\"))","","world.relate(turret, AimsAt(), to: comet)","world.relate(turret, AimsAt(), to: moon)","print(world.targets(AimsAt.self, of: turret) == [moon])","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","","world.despawn(ship)","print(world.contains(turret), world.sources(AimsAt.self, of: moon).isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"false true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Observers of an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that propagates also use the hierarchy: the event moves from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity it was triggered on up to each of its ancestors. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" record changes to relations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and to the hierarchy, to apply after a query or update."}]}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/relatingentities"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Link entities to one another, build trees of parents and children, and query entities by what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they’re linked to."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/children(of:)":{"title":"children(of:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the children of an entity, in the order they were added."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/children(of:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"children","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Entity","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Entity","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/children(of:)","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/CyclicHierarchy":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicHierarchy","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/CyclicHierarchy","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"CyclicHierarchy","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/cyclichierarchy","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error that indicates a link would make an entity its own ancestor."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicHierarchy","kin